 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "빈도 표현 (How often ...?)",
   "en": "Frequency (How often ...?)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "얼마나 자주 하는지는 How often ...?로 묻습니다. 대답에는 every day, once a week, twice a week, three times a week처럼 횟수를 말하거나 often, sometimes, hardly ever, never를 씁니다. 빈도 부사는 일반동사 앞, be동사 뒤에 둡니다.",
   "en": "Ask how often with How often ...? Answer with a count like every day, once a week, twice a week, three times a week, or with often, sometimes, hardly ever or never. Frequency adverbs go before ordinary verbs and after be."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "every day",
     "I study every day."
    ],
    [
     "once / twice / three times a week",
     "I swim twice a week."
    ],
    [
     "often / sometimes / never",
     "I sometimes watch films."
    ],
    [
     "be동사 뒤",
     "He is never late."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "never는 그 자체로 부정이라서 not을 또 쓰지 않아요.",
    "en": "Never is already negative, so don't add not."
   },
   {
    "ko": "횟수 표현은 문장 끝에 와요.",
    "en": "Counts come at the end of the sentence."
   },
   {
    "ko": "be동사 뒤에 빈도 부사: She is often tired.",
    "en": "After be: She is often tired."
   }
  ],
